{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3106","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3106","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3106\",\"parent_revision\":\"1f402923e4fc140ba1450973d3bc50a0b33888df\",\"root_revision\":\"819e548090b338ee47a938ae5a8d9b3c7638e0285d7228d10aeec4d394029de2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item \u2014 its deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict), not a mandate to ship a feature.\\n\\nOrigin: mechanism mined from Claude Code's built-in ultracode Workflow orchestration system \u2014 a code-executed multi-agent workflow runtime whose design contract contains several simple-but-effective patterns DH can adopt without adopting the runtime itself.\\n\\nShared design constraint (same as #3097\u2013#3103): the model keeps the judgment but writes it down once, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists. No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 out of scope.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore schema-validated completion contracts for dispatched agents** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: ultracode Workflow orchestration system\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from the ultracode Workflow system: its agent() calls accept a JSON schema, the subagent is then FORCED to return output through a validated structured-output channel, and validation happens at the tool-call layer so the model retries on mismatch \u2014 the caller receives a validated object, never prose to parse. DH's equivalent boundary is the task-worker completion report, which is a prose STATUS block (STATUS/TASK/FILES_CHANGED/COMMITS/NOTES) that the dispatching agent parses by convention; malformed or partial reports are silently tolerated and each consumer re-implements parsing.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from the ultracode Workflow system: its agent() calls accept a JSON schema, the subagent is then FORCED to return output through a validated structured-output channel, and validation happens at the tool-call layer so the model retries on mismatch \u2014 the caller receives a validated object, never prose to parse. DH's equivalent boundary is the task-worker completion report, which is a prose STATUS block (STATUS/TASK/FILES_CHANGED/COMMITS/NOTES) that the dispatching agent parses by convention; malformed or partial reports are silently tolerated and each consumer re-implements parsing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Mitigates\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nParse ambiguity and silent tolerance of malformed completion reports; per-consumer parsing drift; lost completion data (files/commits/notes that never make it into plan state).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefit Lands In\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe dispatch loop (reads validated objects, not prose), plan state fidelity, and composition with #3098 (a TaskHandoff payload is exactly the kind of object this validation should enforce).\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe dispatch loop (reads validated objects, not prose), plan state fidelity, and composition with #3098 (a TaskHandoff payload is exactly the kind of object this validation should enforce).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Proposed Exploration\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n1. Define a Pydantic CompletionReport model in sam_schema mirroring the current prose STATUS block.\\n2. Route worker completion through an MCP call that validates it (the natural seam is the existing sam_task state-transition path), with validation failure returned to the worker as a retryable error \u2014 the validate-and-retry-at-the-boundary pattern, not trust-and-parse.\\n3. Trial on one plan and count malformed-report incidents caught at the boundary vs the prose baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n1. Define a Pydantic CompletionReport model in sam_schema mirroring the current prose STATUS block.\\n2. Route worker completion through an MCP call that validates it (the natural seam is the existing sam_task state-transition path), with validation failure returned to the worker as a retryable error \u2014 the validate-and-retry-at-the-boundary pattern, not trust-and-parse.\\n3. Trial on one plan and count malformed-report incidents caught at the boundary vs the prose baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3098 (TaskHandoff is the sibling payload; one validation mechanism should serve both); #3099 (a FAILED completion report is the input to failure policy).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a50436ce4080142b077b34ac7b65f2977d636cb5420150afbe775f3911384ac4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIqPxw\"}"}